    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`: `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");`\n- After the owner is successfully saved (so the generated `id` is available), emit an INFO audit line containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe logger name matches what `AuditLogCapture` attaches to (`\"AUDIT\"`), and the formatted message contains all three substrings the test asserts via `anyContains`. The full test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
